Jonadab the Unsightly One wrote:
[> AmEye wrote:]
>> Firstly, it breaks extinction.  
>
> How exactly would pre-generating the levels break
> extinction?  I must be missing something.

Presumably the reasoning is that in 3.4.3, if you hang around on one
dungeon level long enough for 120 of a monster to generate, there won't
be any elsewhere in the dungeon for you to find. If you pregenerate
levels, then monsters will stop generating after you've seen 120 minus
the number of monsters of that type on nonvisited levels, and you'll
have to hunt the remainders down on other levels if you really want to
extinct the species.

The pregenerated version here seems a lot more realistic from the
flavour point of view. However, it is somewhat different from 3.4.3 with
respect to extinctionist play. So it'd definitely be possible to debate
whether the gameplay change would be a good or bad thing in gameplay
terms, independently of the flavour effects (the flavour benefits from
the change, but that isn't reason to make the change if gameplay ends
up ruined as a result).

